      "content": "Losing a self that you thought was permanent is a deep and terrifying form of grief, and it is a profound loss of self that is incredibly heavy to carry alone. \"Fixing\" a self that is deeply hurt is less about immediate repair and more about a slow, deliberate process of self-re-discovery and self-compassion.\n\nInstead of trying to force a \"better self,\" consider what small, quiet things you can do for *you* right now, not for the world or for past perceptions. Can you focus on a routine that is completely self-caring, like a 10-minute walk or a specific comfort for your body, to ground yourself in the present moment.",
